00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.450 align:start position:0%
European Union Finance and economy  ministers will strive this week to forge  a common approach on new rules to  preempt bank crisis the aim is to help a  struggling credit institution or  investment firm to recover from any  shock in an orderly manner preserving  its operations and minimizing the  possibility of taxpayer losses the  proposals concern the single resolution  mechanism and single bank resolution  fund which are a key part of the e use  banking Union they would allow for banks  to be restructured and avoid any shock  liquidation under national insolvency  laws which could harm economic stability  the council will also try to reach a  political agreement on rules governing  savings taxation the proposal would  oblige authorities to exchange  information so that interest payments  made in one nation to people from  another EU state are taxed under the  laws of their country of residence the  goal is to help hide tax evasion The  ministers will also take stock of  efforts to prevent money laundering and  terrorism financing and study a proposal  to simplify value added tax returns  across Europe
 

